# Ghostty configuration.
#
# Lives at the XDG path rather than
# ~/Library/Application Support/com.mitchellh.ghostty/config.ghostty: macOS
# Ghostty reads both, and it MERGES them when both exist — keep only this
# one so there is a single source.
#
# TERMINAL APPEARANCE ONLY. The shell itself — prompt, history, aliases,
# completion, secrets — is global: every terminal and SSH session reads
# ~/.zshrc and ~/.zprofile. Nothing shell-related is set here, so there is
# exactly one obvious place to change the shell: the dotfiles repo's dot_zshrc.
#
{{ $a := output (joinPath .chezmoi.sourceDir "scripts" "theme.py") "appearance" | trim | fromJson -}}
# The colors are not set here at all: the theme line names two GENERATED
# user themes -- dotfiles-light and dotfiles-dark in
# ~/.config/ghostty/themes/ -- rendered at apply time from the same
# vendored palettes every other surface uses. settings.toml at the repo
# root picks the theme names (see docs/theming.md); theme = "system"
# renders the light:/dark: pair Ghostty auto-switches with the OS,
# "light"/"dark" pin one side for the whole stack. The rest of the stack
# follows the same signal: the zsh prompt uses indexed colors 0-15, Neovim
# sets 'background' via lua/bruce/core/appearance.lua, and delta-theme
# (~/.local/bin, wired into git and lazygit) picks the matching syntax
# theme.
theme = {{ if eq $a.mode "system" -}}
light:dotfiles-light,dark:dotfiles-dark
{{- else if eq $a.mode "light" -}}
dotfiles-light
{{- else -}}
dotfiles-dark
{{- end }}
